        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Short R10, R10 for Core2 and CoreS3 / Short R9, R11 for others"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the listed 0-ohm parts are populated as shown, alternate M5Stack GPIO pins are tied together, and the PWM and serial signal paths are connected at the same time. This can cause GPIO contention or interfere with servo control; the exact risk depends on the assembled jumper configuration.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows all alternative 0-ohm GPIO-selection links, as well as links for both PWM and serial signal paths. That conflicts with the specified assembly-time selection of one compatible GPIO mapping and one mutually exclusive servo mode."
